{
  // THE TYPE PROGRAM -- never an emit. Nothing here produces a file: esbuild bundles the
  // plugin and the exporter's core, compiling TypeScript on the way with no help from tsc.
  // This config exists for typescript-eslint, which builds a program from it for the
  // type-aware rules -- the ones in Obsidian's recommended preset that refuse to load without
  // one, and the five no-unsafe-* rules eslint.config.mjs makes errors.
  //
  // INCLUDE NAMES EVERY FILE THOSE RULES LINT, so the program is stated rather than inherited.
  // A file that is only in the program because something else imports it drops out the day
  // that import moves, silently. Named, it stays true by construction.
  //
  // src/core/**/*.ts is the membership engine -- classifiers, predicates, date keys, stable
  // ids: the only TypeScript here, and the part where a wrong type is a wrong shelf rather
  // than a wrong pixel. It is in THIS program so the lint rules read it with the same types
  // the page is read with, and in tsconfig.core.json so tsc checks it under strict.
  //
  // strict IS OFF HERE, ON PURPOSE. esbuild reads `strict` from this file by name and injects
  // "use strict" directives into the bundle from it, so the core's strictness lives in
  // tsconfig.core.json, which extends this one and which esbuild never looks at.
  //
  // allowJs with checkJs off: give the rules a type graph to read, without turning every
  // loose annotation in the page into a lint error.
  //
  // strictFunctionTypes IS ON, alone of the strict family, so this program and the core's
  // agree on what a cast means. Two programs reading one file cannot disagree about that, or
  // every fix for one fails the other. It reports nothing on the JavaScript (checkJs is off)
  // and esbuild does not read it.
  //
  // plugin/**/*.d.ts is the one thing here that is not linted: declarations for the bundler's
  // own `raw:` and `b64:` modules (plugin/bundler-modules.d.ts), which the program needs or
  // every import from them is an error type. eslint.config.mjs ignores them for the same
  // reason -- nothing in one for a rule to read.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": false,
    "strictFunctionTypes": true,
    "types": []
  },
  "include": ["plugin/**/*.js", "plugin/**/*.d.ts", "src/page.js", "src/core/**/*.ts"]
}
